      "utteranceIds": ["a3bb42a1-1ca3-4b1d-8701-e8ed438c728a"],
      "category": "grammar",
      "presentation": "core",
      "title": "aller 的未完成過去時＋原形動詞：正打算進行某事",
      "sourceCueIds": ["c2"],
      "contextCueIds": [],
      "explanation": "「aller（未完成過去時 imparfait）+ 原形動詞」表示過去某個時刻原本「正打算」或「即將」做某事。常與「quand + 複合過去時」連用，說明該意圖被另一突發事件打斷或恰好重合。",
      "sourceSpans": [{"cueId": "c2", "start": 0, "end": 16}]
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "utteranceIds": ["db930fbf-75fa-420a-ad72-2dd669ea6f71"],
      "category": "usage",
      "presentation": "core",
      "title": "patienter un moment 禮貌請求等待",
      "sourceCueIds": ["c3"],
      "contextCueIds": [],
      "explanation": "動詞 patienter 比 attendre 語氣更正式、客氣，常搭配 un moment（片刻、一會兒）用於商務或日常禮貌請求對方稍候。",
      "sourceSpans": [{"cueId": "c3", "start": 12, "end": 30}]
    }
  ],
  "reusableItems": [
